WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:06.340
I believe your day as an entrepreneur is a
pure reflection of your morning rituals.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.340
How you start your day will determine the
type of day you're going to end up having.

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.940
So, one of the most common questions people
ask is, "Pat, I want to know how your day

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.940
starts.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:15.940
What do you do in the morning?

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:16.940
What time do you wake up.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:17.940
What time do you do this?

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:18.940
What time do you do that?"

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.380
So instead of just telling you what I do,
I'll share with you exactly what I do in the

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.380
morning when I wake up.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:27.650
I also went and got a list of people that
I like, how they start their day to give you

00:00:27.650 --> 00:00:30.880
some value and give them some love on their
morning rituals.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:31.880
And this is all entrepreneurs.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.579
And by the way, I want to tell you something
here for you to keep in mind.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:36.370
You can't wing this area.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.870
This is not an area for you to wing.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:38.949
It's very simple.

00:00:38.949 --> 00:00:42.859
This is not an area for you to wing, because
think about it this way.

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:44.559
Everything is by momentum throughout the day.

00:00:44.559 --> 00:00:46.250
It's all about momentum.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.050
So every day is a mountain.

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.790
Every single day is a mountain.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:54.550
This is a mountain here, so meaning you wake
up in the morning and the higher the mountain

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:59.309
goes, the more excited your day starts, the
more the snowball gets thicker and thicker

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:01.149
and thicker, the bigger it gets.

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:02.149
Right?

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:07.070
So you sleep, you're ready, boom you're day
starts, boom boom boom boom, great day.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.110
If you don't have a good start, it's a small
mountain.

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.080
So you don't have a lot of time to create
momentum.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:14.220
It is very important on how you start your
days in the morning.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.870
So, not everybody does the same.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.690
A lot of people have different types of things
they do.

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:23.610
Some are single, some are married, some have
kids, some don't have kids, so you have to

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.160
figure out something that works for you, regardless,
regardless.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.410
One of the most common things I hear from
a lot of people is, you know, for me, I have

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:36.100
to wake up at 10:00 in the morning because
I need to do this, this, that.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.270
If you don't get your morning ritual down,
and you have any desire to compete as an entrepreneur,

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.180
you are toast.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.770
If you think you're going to be able to compete
with the rest of the guys in the world of

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:47.770
business.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:48.770
So let's go through a few of them here.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.920
The first one, I want to give some love to
Gary Vee.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.980
Here's what I like what Gary Vee says on his
morning ritual.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:58.860
He wakes up at 6:00 AM, reads the new in the
bathroom [something I do as well], and before

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:02.960
leaving the house he hugs his kids for five
minutes and calls a family member while driving.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:03.960
I like that.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.490
Hugs his kids for five minutes and calls a
family member while driving.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.000
Gary, props to you for doing that.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Tony Robbins.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.180
Tony Robbins has a very good ritual.

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:15.240
He doesn't have a specific time that he wakes
up, because of the traveling that he does.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.990
He may be in Europe, he may be here, so he
doesn't have an "I wake up exactly at 4:45

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.770
or 5:50" or whatever.

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.280
He doesn't have that.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:23.590
So he doesn't have a time for that.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:29.390
He wakes up, he does a cold plunge, submerge
for a full minute, under water, cold, cold

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:33.720
water, if you've ever done one of these cold
dips, is what he does, and the primes of his

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.140
days, what he calls the primes of his days,
three things.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.510
One, he has a breaking exercise that he does.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:42.780
If you see it, it's a very -- if you haven't
seen the Tony Robbins documentary, I highly

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.670
recommend you watch the Tony Robbins documentary.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:47.070
I don't even know what it's called.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:51.780
but I do know if you go on Netflix, and you
type in Tony Robbins documentary, it will

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.780
come up.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.020
I highly recommend you watch it.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.020
It's solid.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.610
It shows how some of his events are.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.610
It's "I'm Not Your Guru."

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.360
That's what the documentary is called.

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.360
Phenomenal.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.270
And you kind of see a day of his life from
what it looks like.

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:07.650
But the prime of his day he has his breathing
exercise, you'll see how he does it.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.410
You may not do it, but that's his.

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.170
Expressing gratitude, and prayer.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:17.740
He's big on prayer, on what he does, which
is pretty interesting.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:21.770
His day is probably one of the most energetic
people around the world that if you go to

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:26.080
his convention, you see him with his five,
10,000 people that he has.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.730
Everybody is fired up, because his energy
gets everybody else fired up.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:36.080
You have more of a possibility of impacting
people's lives if your energy is higher.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.950
Morning ritual is purely an energy game is
what you've got to keep in mind.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:39.950
Zuckerberg.

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:40.950
Let's see what Zuckerberg does.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.870
This is a guy that's worth 40 some billion,
somewhere around there.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.099
He wakes up at 8:00 a.m.

00:03:47.099 --> 00:03:48.099
Interesting.

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:51.240
Not a lot -- you hear 5:00, he's an 8:00 a.m-er.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.370
When he hasn't been working all night, so
he's a guy that works all night til 2:00,

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.890
3:00 in the morning, but he wakes up at 8:00
a.m.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:59.840
He wears the exact same shirt every single
day because he doesn't want to spend a lot

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:03.030
of time thinking about what to wear, and so
that's what he does.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.910
Jack Dorsey, founder of Twitter and Square.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:09.620
He wakes up at 5:30 to meditate, followed
by a six-mile jog.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.860
Pretty intense.

00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.260
Richard Branson, from Virgin group.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.739
He is generally on his island.

00:04:16.739 --> 00:04:21.329
He swims around the island or goes kite surfing
it it's windy.

00:04:21.329 --> 00:04:24.380
He then plays tennis before sitting down for
a healthy breakfast.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:28.620
He doesn't have a set time when he wakes up;
he leaves his curtains open and it's where

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.850
exactly the sun rises.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:32.870
He says, when the sun rises, the light wakes
me up.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:38.530
So he doesn't have an alarm clock, but typically
the sun rises at 5:45, 6:00 in the morning.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:42.000
Simon Cowell -- we don't know what time he
wakes up.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.100
He may be waking up about 11:00 in the morning
but he does say what he does in the morning.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:50.810
He resets the snooze button twice, before
being served a breakfast of hot water with

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:56.210
lemon, papaya juice with lime, oatmeal, tea,
and three smoothies.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.690
Pretty specific.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.270
And knowing his personality, I can actually
see him doing that every single day.

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.900
Tory Burch, the designer.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:06.370
She's worth around a billion, a little shy
of a billion dollars.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:13.010
Wakes up at 5:45 a.m., immediately checks
her work emails, gets her three boys out of

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:17.449
bed and takes a 45 minute exercise such as
a quick walk.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:18.449
Now that's her routine.

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:21.610
Let me tell you what I do when I wake up in
the morning.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:22.610
Okay.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:25.060
So, before I tell you what I do when I wake
up in the morning, you've got to keep in mind,

00:05:25.060 --> 00:05:27.700
I have three kids all under the age of five.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:32.550
I'm married, I have three kids all under the
age of five, I run a company with a ton of

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:36.220
employees and thousands of agents around the
country selling insurance, annuities, and

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:37.220
investment products.

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.960
The company is called PHP Agency.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.760
Now that's what I do as a business, right?

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:47.350
So, one of the things for me, just a couple
of months back, three, four, five months back,

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:53.460
my dad -- if there's one thing my dad will
not hesitate to do -- my dad will pull me

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:56.740
aside and he'll say, "Hey, Mr. Body Builder.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:57.740
What happened to your six-pack?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.310
Now you have a one-pack."

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:01.820
He has no filters.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.570
If you're out of shape, he'll tell you.

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:07.300
Okay, he's good with the ladies; he won't
tell that to the ladies, but he will tell

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.780
me, if I"m out of shape, he'll tell me.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:12.900
Now I love that because I'd rather have the
truth than you trying to make me feel good

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:15.770
as a father, as a mentor.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:19.500
So I get on the scale, I weigh 256 is what
I weigh.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.540
I've never weighed 256 before.

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:26.850
The moment I noticed myself weighing 256,
my energy goes high, my energy goes low, and

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:30.949
this was right around when the baby was born.

00:06:30.949 --> 00:06:33.889
And when a baby is born, you're doing two
hours of sleep, you're waking up and doing

00:06:33.889 --> 00:06:34.889
all this other stuff.

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:36.949
No matter what happens, I feel it.

00:06:36.949 --> 00:06:42.580
The moment I feel the energy dropping, the
moment I feel it, I know, because I can't

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:45.400
hang till 10:00 11:00 if I'm starting early.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.400
I know that.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.153
And my business requires me to hang for a
long time because it requires that I have

00:06:49.153 --> 00:06:50.710
a lot of energy.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:53.180
So there is a formula for every single person.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:57.080
This isn't something - you need to ask yourself
how is your energy in the morning, and how

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:58.259
is your energy in the afternoon.

00:06:58.259 --> 00:07:01.970
And can you hang longer, or by 5:00, 6:00,
you're already tired.

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:05.770
Keep in mind, your competitors wake up typically
earlier than you, and they are able to last

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.770
longer than you.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:09.270
That's the only reason they're growing faster
than you and having a bigger business than

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:12.010
you, whatever type of a business they have
in place.

00:07:12.010 --> 00:07:13.110
That is if you're competitive.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:14.509
Here's my morning.

00:07:14.509 --> 00:07:19.860
I wake up generally at 4:30 - 4:45 a.m., and
have training sessions at 5:00.

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:24.759
If I have a training session with my trainers
at 6:00, I'm up 5:15.

00:07:24.759 --> 00:07:28.490
This morning I had a training session at 6:00;
I can no longer help myself.

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.229
It's a 4:45 wake up.

00:07:30.229 --> 00:07:35.870
At 4:45 I wake up, I'll check my email, I'll
go through all the information that I have

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:41.259
on my email, I'll typically listen to an audio
book, while I'm driving or walking around.

00:07:41.259 --> 00:07:45.610
I will do my daily affirmations on what I
tell myself.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.160
It's been one of my rituals for a long, long
time.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.690
I have my affirmations laminated all over
the wall.

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:56.030
They are all over my shower wall, everywhere
on what I tell myself.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.030
Then I go to the gym.

00:07:57.030 --> 00:08:00.350
I do my routine, I do my workout in the morning,
weights.

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:03.210
Right after that, one of the things that I've
been doing recently that I love, let me tell

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:07.430
you, this is a very fascinating thing, if
you have the luxury of doing this.

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:12.500
I'm 6'5", 240, so my back and my knees feel
it a lot, especially when I was in the Army,

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.949
we used to ruck march, with 50 pound backpacks.

00:08:15.949 --> 00:08:20.919
It's what we used to do, right?

00:08:20.919 --> 00:08:27.919
So, cryotherapy, is something I've started
doing recently.

00:08:27.919 --> 00:08:32.510
You literally stand there, with no shirt on,
no clothes on, and you stand there, and this

00:08:32.510 --> 00:08:35.800
thing starts and it goes all the way down
to minus 240.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:40.680
And the system I use -- there are many different
ones, these machines run around $100,000 - it

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.459
goes to minus 240 for three minutes.

00:08:43.459 --> 00:08:48.820
By the time you're done, what happens to the
blood, the entire body, is flexible.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:53.342
It feels like a million bucks, and your body
gets shocked, is what it does.

00:08:53.342 --> 00:08:58.380
Now I do this at 6:00 in the morning, so it
works very, very effectively.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:00.940
If you can do that at your gym, it's great.

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.311
Even if you do it once a week, I highly recommend
it for you to try cryotherapy.

00:09:03.311 --> 00:09:08.290
A good breakfast, you have to have a good
breakfast, because that's your gas tank.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:14.380
So remember, if you go and do 10 miles, 20
miles, 200 miles in your car, you need to

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.990
go to a gas station.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:18.310
Breakfast meals are your gas stations.

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:19.630
You need to go fill up the tank.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.100
Then I do my thinking.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:24.080
These are the times that I do my thinking,
I do my strategy sessions.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.640
I do my ideation.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:30.339
I think about what I'm working on, my next
project, what needs help, what needs to be

00:09:30.339 --> 00:09:31.339
improved.

00:09:31.339 --> 00:09:35.400
Who do I need to call, what is my conversation
going to sound like, what am I going to do

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:37.230
with this, what am I going to do with that,
so it's thinking.

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:39.330
A lot of thinking and strategy.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:45.640
And praying, definitely praying and meditating,
catching up on news.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:49.640
If my kids wake up early, they'll typically
wake up at 6:45ish.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:54.420
I'm typically gone by then, but I play with
them when I get home.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.730
And so that's typical with what my days look
like in the morning.

00:09:56.730 --> 00:10:01.880
Now one thing I'm going to tell you to give
you some feedback on -- this is Monday - Saturday

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.920
of what my schedule looks like.

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:05.620
Sundays, playday.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:07.970
Family day, fun day.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:14.010
You know, there is nothing on Sunday going
on, but me doing whatever I can to have fun

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.529
with my kids.

00:10:15.529 --> 00:10:18.380
I look forward to Sundays because we have
a great time together.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:21.280
We play together, we enjoy each other's company.

00:10:21.280 --> 00:10:23.320
My wife and I have a great time together.

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:27.690
We either swim in the pool or go and do all
these other things that we do on a Sunday.

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:29.301
There's no set thing on what to do on Sunday.

00:10:29.301 --> 00:10:34.500
Sunday is refueling, re-energizing, re-firing
yourself up.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:39.130
Then at night, there is a lot of preparation
for the week, typically a couple of hours

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:40.670
of preparation for the week.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:43.610
And then we start the day back up again the
next day.

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:48.300
I typically will do a Facebook Mentions on
Sunday night at 10:00, 9:00 recently to do

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:52.890
some Q&amp;A, with other entrepreneurs from all
around the world, and that's what my week

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:53.890
looks like.

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:56.130
Every week, there's one thing I want to tell
you guys.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:00.500
If you can't do it every week, I do recommend
it every other week -- especially if your

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:06.420
body is in action, get a massage every other
week, minimum.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:09.760
Even if it's $60, a dollar a minute, I highly
recommend it.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:14.180
Get a massage, every other week, minimum.

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:16.610
This body that you have, you and I live in
it, right?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.850
We live in this body.

00:11:17.850 --> 00:11:19.040
Let me explain.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.270
We are not the body.

00:11:21.270 --> 00:11:22.450
We are the spirit.

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.110
We're the mind, right?

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:26.000
We live in this body.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:30.080
We need to take care of this body, and then
it gives us a lot of miles.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.080
It's like a car.

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:35.990
You buy a car, you know, you drive in the
car, but you're not the car.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:38.010
I don't know if I'm making any sense.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:41.580
You're in the car, you're driving the car,
but you're not the car.

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:46.029
The driver dictates how long that car can
last.

00:11:46.029 --> 00:11:53.020
You, the body is the car, but your mind, the
heart, we, the spirit, are the driver.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.779
The way you take care of this, this is going
to last a long time.

00:11:55.779 --> 00:12:00.730
Now obviously, we cannot unfortunately do
anything at this point with some of the health

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:03.870
things that happen, cancer and all these other
things that you don't have control of.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:10.160
But you can definitely control energy, weight,
being able to last, being able to do whatever

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.910
you can for your body to have more endurance,
more stamina.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.050
